{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/255373-setting-hack-instincts","id":255373,"title":"Setting Hack - Instincts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-12T10:02:22-07:00","id":255373,"title":"Setting Hack - Instincts","content":"The Created aren't natural, yes? To be promethean is to be in some sort of transitory state - less than human, more than a corpse. Their instincts, refined by the azoth that animates their body, guide them towards mortality. If they choose to follow them. If they survive.<br /> <br /> In this setting hack, the azoth itself sometimes communicates with the Created - and not just in the guise of the qashmallim. The Created see and hear and feel things, people and places of significance to the pyros and to their own pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> These urgings of the azoth and its underlying Principle are never experienced with any sort of context as to why they might be important to a promethean's pilgrimage. Quite often, the Created are confused as to the meaning of their instincts; they only know that following them might (*might*) lead them a little closer to the New Dawn. More often than not, a Created's instincts urge them to put themselves into danger by interacting with mortals, other prometheans or worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> In terms of plot of story, a promethean's instincts are vague feelings and perceptions that exist to provide the storyteller with ammunition, helping to integrate the characters into plots. Instincts serve as starting points for stories. A Created feels that some human he meets is in some way significant to his Pilgrimage --&gt; he feels drawn to observe/interact with the human --&gt; plot happens.<br /> <br /> Instincts often encourage interaction with humans. The pilgrimage is about reaching some sort of understanding of what being human means, which requires being around people.<br /> <br /> Instincts aren't perfectly reliable, and never entirely accurate. Instincts aren't a milestone detector, but they might sometimes provide clues to follow.<br /> <br /> A promethean's instincts can be tampered with. There should be ways for antagonists (followers of Mercurius, alchemists, Qashmallim etc.) to influence the way a promethean feels about his pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> Prometheans are in no way mystically bound to follow the demands of their instincts; and might, in many situations, choose not to do so. They should be used by the storyteller to force dilemmas concerning priorities - follow your instinct and make progress on your pilgrimage or focus on other goals (power, survival, the throng, etc.)?<br /> <br /> At no way in a character's pilgrimage do the instincts ever stop making themselves noticeable. Every Refuser and every Centimani can still feel people and places significant to his New Dawn, even if he refuses to interact with them every single time. It's always there, reminding them that they could, potentially, work towards becoming human, if they chose to do so.<br /> <br /> Although it is assumed that a Created's instincts are in some way related to azoth and to the Principle, there doesn't necessarily need to be a connection. It usually serves the story to preserve the mystery of the Principle. Sometimes a Qashmallim's mission involves telling a promethean to go *against* his instincts.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T12:50:16-07:00","id":255509,"title":"","content":"Like it .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T20:08:11-07:00","id":255756,"title":"","content":"Elpis. You're describing the Elpis Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T00:53:41-07:00","id":255880,"title":"","content":"Not at all, no. Elpis is 1) an optional merit and not an intrinsic aspect of the Promethean condition that every Created possesses and 2) requires sleep, a trance or an intentional attempt to gain visions. Instincts just happen, without any effort on the part of the Created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 09-13-2014, 03:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","va